[51.317208, "o", "Chunks count: 209, Passages count: 209\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0000:\r\nptext (repr): ' risk of potential drug-drug interactions for an individual patient can be appropriately managed\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): ' the risk of potential drug-drug interactions for an individual patient can be appropriately managed'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0001:\r\nptext (repr): 'lts who are at high risk for progression to severe COVID-19, including hospitalization or death.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): ' adults who are at high risk for progression to severe COVID-19, including hospitalization or death.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0002:\r\n"]
[51.317256, "o", "ptext (repr): 's not approved for use as pre-exposure or post-exposure prophylaxis for prevention of COVID-19 .\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'ID is not approved for use as pre-exposure or post-exposure prophylaxis for prevention of COVID-19 .'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0003:\r\nptext (repr): 'with or without food . The tablets should be swallowed whole and not chewed, broken, or crushed.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'ken with or without food . The tablets should be swallowed whole and not chewed, broken, or crushed.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0004:\r\nptext (repr): ') with all 3 tablets taken together orally twice daily in the morning and at bedtime for 5 days.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'blet) with all 3 tablets taken together orally twice daily in the morning and at bedtime for 5 days.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0005:\r\nptext (repr): 'ed after hemodialysis .\\nTable 1: Recommended Dose and Regimen for Patients with Renal Impairment\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'stered after hemodialysis .\\nTable 1: Recommended Dose and Regimen for Patients with Renal Impairment'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0006:\r\nptext (repr): 'roximately the same time each day for 5 days.\\nModerate renal impairment (eGFR ≥30 to <60 mL/min)\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): ' approximately the same time each day for 5 days.\\nModerate renal impairment (eGFR ≥30 to <60 mL/min)'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0007:\r\nptext (repr): 'modialysis\\nOn days of hemodialysis, the PAXLOVID dose should be administered after hemodialysis.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'g hemodialysis\\nOn days of hemodialysis, the PAXLOVID dose should be administered after hemodialysis.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0008:\r\nptext (repr): 'Day 1\\n300 mg nirmatrelvir (two 150 mg tablets) with 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 mg tablet) once\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'Day 1\\n300 mg nirmatrelvir (two 150 mg tablets) with 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 mg tablet) once'\r\n"]
[51.317332, "o", "Mismatch for PASSAGE_0009:\r\n"]
[51.317353, "o", "ptext (repr): '2-5\\n150 mg nirmatrelvir (one 150 mg tablet) with 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 mg tablet) once daily\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'ays 2-5\\n150 mg nirmatrelvir (one 150 mg tablet) with 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 mg tablet) once daily'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0010:\r\nptext (repr): 'ent; therefore, PAXLOVID is not recommended for use in patients with severe hepatic impairment .\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'airment; therefore, PAXLOVID is not recommended for use in patients with severe hepatic impairment .'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0011:\r\nptext (repr): 'niquely identified by the color, shape, and debossing. Each tablet contains 100 mg of ritonavir.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'ts uniquely identified by the color, shape, and debossing. Each tablet contains 100 mg of ritonavir.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0012:\r\nptext (repr): \"ne conductance regulator potentiators: lumacaftor/ivacaftor\\n- Herbal products: St. John's Wort (\\n\\n||\"\r\nchunk (repr): \"mbrane conductance regulator potentiators: lumacaftor/ivacaftor\\n- Herbal products: St. John's Wort (\"\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0013:\r\nptext (repr): 'isk of potential drug-drug interactions for an individual patient can be appropriately managed .\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'he risk of potential drug-drug interactions for an individual patient can be appropriately managed .'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0014:\r\nptext (repr): 'r, immediately discontinue PAXLOVID and initiate appropriate medications and/or supportive care.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'occur, immediately discontinue PAXLOVID and initiate appropriate medications and/or supportive care.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0015:\r\nptext (repr): 'PAXLOVID to patients with pre-existing liver diseases, liver enzyme abnormalities, or hepatitis.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'ing PAXLOVID to patients with pre-existing liver diseases, liver enzyme abnormalities, or hepatitis.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0016:\r\nptext (repr): 'nce to HIV protease inhibitors in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection .\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'istance to HIV protease inhibitors in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection .'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0017:\r\nptext (repr): 'nificant adverse reactions are described elsewhere in the labeling:\\n- Hypersensitivity reactions\\n\\n||'\r\n"]
[51.317371, "o", "chunk (repr): ' significant adverse reactions are described elsewhere in the labeling:\\n- Hypersensitivity reactions'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0018:\r\nptext (repr): ': Abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting\\nGeneral Disorders and Administration Site Conditions: Malaise\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'ders: Abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting\\nGeneral Disorders and Administration Site Conditions: Malaise'\r\n"]
[51.31738, "o", "Mismatch for PASSAGE_0019:\r\n"]
[51.31746, "o", "ptext (repr): 'her CYP3A substrates may require a dose adjustment or additional monitoring as shown in Table 2.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'h other CYP3A substrates may require a dose adjustment or additional monitoring as shown in Table 2.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0020:\r\nptext (repr): 'crease nirmatrelvir and ritonavir plasma concentrations and reduce PAXLOVID therapeutic effect .\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'y decrease nirmatrelvir and ritonavir plasma concentrations and reduce PAXLOVID therapeutic effect .'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0021:\r\nptext (repr): 'tion on dosing or monitoring with concomitant use of a strong CYP3A inhibitor such as ritonavir.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'ormation on dosing or monitoring with concomitant use of a strong CYP3A inhibitor such as ritonavir.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0022:\r\n"]
[51.31751, "o", "ptext (repr): '↑ alfuzosin\\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential hypotension .\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): '↑ alfuzosin\\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential hypotension .'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0023:\r\nptext (repr): '↑ tamsulosin\\nAvoid concomitant use with PAXLOVID.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): '↑ tamsulosin\\nAvoid concomitant use with PAXLOVID.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0024:\r\nptext (repr): '-administration contraindicated due to potential for serious and/or life-threatening reactions .\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'e\\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for serious and/or life-threatening reactions .'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0025:\r\nptext (repr): '↑ antiarrhythmic\\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for cardiac arrhythmias .\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): '↑ antiarrhythmic\\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for cardiac arrhythmias .'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0026:\r\nptext (repr): 'ranted and therapeutic concentration monitoring is recommended for antiarrhythmics if available.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): ' warranted and therapeutic concentration monitoring is recommended for antiarrhythmics if available.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0027:\r\nptext (repr): 'nistration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance .\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance .'\r\n"]
[51.317582, "o", "Mismatch for PASSAGE_0028:\r\nptext (repr): 'ib, encorafenib,ibrutinib, ivosidenib, neratinib, nilotinib, venetoclax,vinblastine, vincristine\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'atinib, encorafenib,ibrutinib, ivosidenib, neratinib, nilotinib, venetoclax,vinblastine, vincristine'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0029:\r\nptext (repr): 'al side effects.\\nFor further information, refer to individual product label for anticancer drug.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'stinal side effects.\\nFor further information, refer to individual product label for anticancer drug.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0030:\r\nptext (repr): 'ly monitor international normalized ratio (INR) if co-administration with warfarin is necessary.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'losely monitor international normalized ratio (INR) if co-administration with warfarin is necessary.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0031:\r\nptext (repr): 'Avoid concomitant use.\\ndabigatranSee Pharmacokinetics, Clinical Drug Interaction Studies (12.3).\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'an. Avoid concomitant use.\\ndabigatranSee Pharmacokinetics, Clinical Drug Interaction Studies (12.3).'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0032:\r\nptext (repr): 'igatran or avoid concomitant use. Refer to the dabigatran product label for further information.\\n\\n||'\r\n"]
[51.317599, "o", "chunk (repr): ' dabigatran or avoid concomitant use. Refer to the dabigatran product label for further information.'\r\n"]
[51.317674, "o", "Mismatch for PASSAGE_0033:\r\nptext (repr): ' PAXLOVID depend on the apixaban dose. Refer to the apixaban product label for more information.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'with PAXLOVID depend on the apixaban dose. Refer to the apixaban product label for more information.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0034:\r\nptext (repr): 'nistration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance .\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance .'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0035:\r\nptext (repr): 'needed for clonazepam when co-administered with PAXLOVID and clinical monitoring is recommended.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): ' be needed for clonazepam when co-administered with PAXLOVID and clinical monitoring is recommended.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0036:\r\nptext (repr): ' and active metabolite hydroxy-bupropion\\nMonitor for an adequate clinical response to bupropion.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'pion and active metabolite hydroxy-bupropion\\nMonitor for an adequate clinical response to bupropion.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0037:\r\nptext (repr): 'ose of trazodone should be considered. Refer to trazadone product label for further information.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'er dose of trazodone should be considered. Refer to trazadone product label for further information.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0038:\r\nptext (repr): '↓ voriconazole\\nAvoid concomitant use of voriconazole.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): '↓ voriconazole\\nAvoid concomitant use of voriconazole.'\r\nMismatch for PASSAGE_0039:\r\nptext (repr): ' ketoconazole, isavuconazonium sulfate, and itraconazole product labels for further information.\\n\\n||'\r\nchunk (repr): 'r to ketoconazole, isavuconazonium sulfate, and itraconazole product labels for further information.'"]
