[98.847893, "o", "PASSAGE_0019 (Heading: 7.1\tPotential for PAXLOVID to Affect Other Drugs):\r\n  PAXLOVID (nirmatrelvir co-packaged with ritonavir) is a strong inhibitor of CYP3A, and an inhibitor of CYP2D6, P-gp and \r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0021 (Heading: 7.3\tEstablished and Other Potentially Significant ):\r\n  Table 2 provides a listing of clinically significant drug interactions, including contraindicated drugs . Drugs listed i\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0022 (Heading: ↑ alfuzosin):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential hypotension .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0024 (Heading: ↑ ranolazine):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for serious and/or life-threatening reactions .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0025 (Heading: ↑ antiarrhythmic):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for cardiac arrhythmias .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0027 (Heading: ↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0034 (Heading: ↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0041 (Heading: ↑ colchicine):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for serious and/or life-threatening reactions in patients with renal \r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0045 (Heading: ↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance. Alternate antimyc\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0048 (Heading: ↑ lurasidone↑ pimozide):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to serious and/or life-threatening reactions such as cardiac arrhythmias .\r\n"]
[98.848002, "o", "----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0051 (Heading: ↑ silodosin):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for postural hypotension .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0054 (Heading: ↑ eplerenone):\r\n  Co-administration with eplerenone is contraindicated due to potential for hyperkalemia .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0055 (Heading: ↑ ivabradine):\r\n  Co-administration with ivabradine is contraindicated due to potential for bradycardia or conduction disturbances .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0059 (Heading: ↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance .\r\n"]
[98.848053, "o", "----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0063 (Heading: ↑ dihydroergotamine↑ ergotamine↑ methylergonovine):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for acute ergot toxicity characterized by vasospasm and ischemia of t\r\n----------------------------------------\r\n"]
[98.848142, "o", "PASSAGE_0068 (Heading: ↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0069 (Heading: ↑ lovastatin↑ simvastatin):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for myopathy including rhabdomyolysis .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0072 (Heading: ↑ voclosporin):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for acute and/or chronic nephrotoxicity .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0079 (Heading: ↑ lomitapide):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for hepatotoxicity and gastrointestinal adverse reactions .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0080 (Heading: ↑ eletriptan):\r\n"]
[98.848165, "o", "  Co-administration of eletriptan within at least 72 hours of PAXLOVID is contraindicated due to potential for serious adv\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0081 (Heading: ↑ ubrogepant):\r\n  Co-administration of ubrogepant with PAXLOVID is contraindicated due to potential for serious adverse reactions .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0083 (Heading: ↑ finerenone):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for serious adverse reactions including hyperkalemia, hypotension, an\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0089 (Heading: ↑ naloxegol):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to the potential for opioid withdrawal symptoms .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0090 (Heading: ↑ sildenafil):\r\n  Co-administration of sildenafil with PAXLOVID is contraindicated for use in pulmonary hypertension due to the potential \r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0095 (Heading: ↑ triazolam↑ midazolam):"]
[98.848221, "o", "\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for extreme sedation and respiratory depression .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0098 (Heading: ↑ flibanserin):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for hypotension, syncope, and CNS depression .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nPASSAGE_0099 (Heading: ↑ tolvaptan):\r\n  Co-administration contraindicated due to potential for dehydration, hypovolemia and hyperkalemia .\r\n----------------------------------------\r\n"]
