[219.789366, "o", "QUOTE NOT FOUND in 4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85 PASSAGE_0001!\r\nQuote: 'Lopinavir and ritonavir oral solution must be taken with food.'\r\nChunk: '2.1 General Administration Recommendations\\nLopinavir\\xa0and ritonavir oral solution must be taken with food.'...\r\nQUOTE NOT FOUND in 4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85 PASSAGE_0005!\r\nQuote: '80 mg/20 mg per mL Oral Solution 400 mg/100 mg (5 mL) twice daily'\r\nChunk: 'Recommended Dosage\\n80 mg/20 mg per mL Oral Solution 400 mg/100 mg (5 mL)\\xa0twice daily\\nThe dose of lopinavir and ritonavir must be increased when administered in combination with efavirenz, nevirapine o'...\r\nQUOTE NOT FOUND in 4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85 PASSAGE_0014!\r\nQuote: 'Initiation of lopinavir and ritonavir, a CYP3A inhibitor, in patients receiving medications metabolized by CYP3A or initiation of medications metabolized by CYP3A in patients already receiving lopinavir and ritonavir, may increase plasma concentrations of medications metabolized by CYP3A.'\r\nChunk: '5.1 Risk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions\\nInitiation of lopinavir and ritonavir, a CYP3A inhibitor, in patients receiving medications metabolized by CYP3A or initiation of medicat'...\r\nQUOTE NOT FOUND in 4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85 PASSAGE_0016!\r\n"]
[219.789422, "o", "Quote: 'Pancreatitis has been observed in patients receiving lopinavir and ritonavir therapy, including those who developed marked triglyceride elevations.'\r\nChunk: '5.3 Pancreatitis\\nPancreatitis has been observed in patients receiving lopinavir\\xa0and ritonavir therapy, including those who developed marked triglyceride elevations. In some cases, fatalities have been'...\r\nQUOTE NOT FOUND in 4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85 PASSAGE_0018!\r\nQuote: 'Postmarketing cases of QT interval prolongation and torsade de pointes have been reported although causality of lopinavir and ritonavir could not be established.'\r\nChunk: '5.5 QT Interval Prolongation\\nPostmarketing cases of QT interval prolongation and torsade de pointes have been reported although causality of lopinavir\\xa0and ritonavir could not be established. Avoid use'...\r\nQUOTE NOT FOUND in 4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85 PASSAGE_0019!\r\n"]
[219.789434, "o", "Quote: 'Lopinavir and ritonavir prolongs the PR interval in some patients. Cases of second or third degree atrioventricular block have been reported.'\r\n"]
[219.789511, "o", "Chunk: '5.6 PR Interval Prolongation\\nLopinavir\\xa0and ritonavir prolongs the PR interval in some patients. Cases of second or third degree atrioventricular block have been reported. Lopinavir\\xa0and ritonavir shoul'...\r\nQUOTE NOT FOUND in 4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85 PASSAGE_0022!\r\nQuote: 'Treatment with lopinavir and ritonavir has resulted in large increases in the concentration of total cholesterol and triglycerides .'\r\nChunk: '5.9 Lipid Elevations\\nTreatment with lopinavir\\xa0and ritonavir has resulted in large increases in the concentration of total cholesterol and triglycerides . Triglyceride and cholesterol testing should be'...\r\nQUOTE NOT FOUND in 4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85 PASSAGE_0014!\r\nQuote: 'Initiation of lopinavir and ritonavir, a CYP3A inhibitor, in patients receiving medications metabolized by CYP3A or initiation of medications metabolized by CYP3A in patients already receiving lopinavir and ritonavir, may increase plasma concentrations of medications metabolized by CYP3A.'\r\nChunk: '5.1 Risk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions\\nInitiation of lopinavir and ritonavir, a CYP3A inhibitor, in patients receiving medications metabolized by CYP3A or initiation of medicat'...\r\nQUOTE NOT FOUND in 4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85 PASSAGE_0015!\r\nQuote: 'Lopinavir and ritonavir oral solution should not be used in preterm neonates in the immediate postnatal period because of possible toxicities.'\r\nChunk: '5.2 Toxicity in Preterm Neonates\\nLopinavir and ritonavir oral solution contains the excipients ethanol, approximately 42% (v/v) and propylene glycol, approximately 15% (w/v). When administered concomi'...\r\nQUOTE NOT FOUND in 4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85 PASSAGE_0017!\r\nQuote: 'Appropriate laboratory testing should be conducted prior to initiating therapy with lopinavir and ritonavir and patients should be monitored closely during treatment.'\r\nChunk: '5.4 Hepatotoxicity\\nPatients with underlying hepatitis B or C or marked elevations in transaminase prior to treatment may be at increased risk for developing or worsening of transaminase elevations or '...\r\nQUOTE NOT FOUND in 4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85 PASSAGE_0019!\r\nQuote: 'Lopinavir and ritonavir should be used with caution in patients with underlying structural heart disease, pre-existing conduction system abnormalities, ischemic heart disease or cardiomyopathies'\r\nChunk: '5.6 PR Interval Prolongation\\nLopinavir\\xa0and ritonavir prolongs the PR interval in some patients. Cases of second or third degree atrioventricular block have been reported. Lopinavir\\xa0and ritonavir shoul'...\r\nQUOTE NOT FOUND in 4b1caefa-e6a2-42f3-9194-6dc1dd9e6d85 PASSAGE_0022!\r\nQuote: 'Triglyceride and cholesterol testing should be performed prior to initiating lopinavir and ritonavir therapy and at periodic intervals during therapy.'\r\n"]
[219.789532, "o", "Chunk: '5.9 Lipid Elevations\\nTreatment with lopinavir\\xa0and ritonavir has resulted in large increases in the concentration of total cholesterol and triglycerides . Triglyceride and cholesterol testing should be'...\r\nSome quotes failed verification!\r\n"]
[219.79151, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@15b83e10b8d1:/workspace# "]
[228.58223, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > test_normalize.py\nimport re\n\ndef get_exact_substring(chunk, target_text):\n    # Normalize whitespaces to a single space, including non-breaking spaces\n    def normalize(text):\n        return re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text).strip().lower()\n    \n    norm_chunk = normalize(chunk)\n    norm_target = normalize(target_text)\n    \n    if norm_target not in norm_chunk:\n        print(f\"Target NOT found in normalized chunk!\")\n        print(f\"Norm Target: {repr(norm_target)}\")\n        print(f\"Norm Chunk:  {repr(norm_chunk[:200])}\")\n        return None\n    \n    # We want to find the start and end indices of the match in the original chunk\n    # Let's do a character-by-character search or regex search\n    # Since regex can be tricky with special chars, let's build a regex from target_text\n    # where each whitespace is replaced by \\s+\n    escaped = re.escape(target_text)\n    # Replace escaped spaces with \\s+\n    pattern = re.sub(r'\\\\\\s+', r'\\s+', escaped)\n    # Also allow non-breaking spaces and other spaces\n    pattern = pattern.replace(' ', r'\\s+')\n    \n    match = re.search(pattern, chunk, re.IGNORECASE)\n    if match:\n        return match.group(0)\n    return None\n\nchunk = \"Treatment with lopinavir\\xa0and ritonavir has resulted in large increases\"\ntarget = \"Treatment with lopinavir and ritonavir has resulted\"\nprint(repr(get_exact_substring(chunk, target)))\nEOF\npython3 test_normalize.py\n"]
[228.582466, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > test_normalize.py"]
